1
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:12,940
Brighten up the peace,
then step away and see.

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,460
Like someone calling out
after the rain has stopped.

3
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:35,320
Holding my mom's hand as we walked,
looking back over our shoulders.

4
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:42,480
That strange feeling I felt back then.

5
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:47,740
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:53,520
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,920 --> 00:00:59,680
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,680 --> 00:01:01,840
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:05,820
Politicians with their self-important faces,

10
00:01:05,820 --> 00:01:09,100
and the blue-tinted aunties
who are a thorn in your side,

11
00:01:09,620 --> 00:01:12,100
try turning the corner.

12
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,700
That corner there.

13
00:01:15,740 --> 00:01:19,900
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

14
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,500
Over there is Kame-ari.

15
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,840
Surely, Kame-ari.

16
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:33,080
Everyone, come on over to our town!

17
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:34,600
Thank you.

18
00:01:36,740 --> 00:01:39,580
Bonus Battle 4

19
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,900
Is everyone here?

20
00:01:54,900 --> 00:01:57,020
No, the fishmonger hasn't arrived yet.

21
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,600
Sorry I'm late.

22
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,620
Did your wife run out on you again?

23
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:09,000
If my wife fails to collect the debts this year,
of all years,

24
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,420
she says she'll divorce me,
then goes and leaves the kids behind!

25
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:14,240
That's rough.

26
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,060
We really have to do
something about it this year!

27
00:02:19,340 --> 00:02:21,800
Now then, the 27th

28
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:28,840
What are you listening to, senpai?

29
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,760
It's probably horse
racing or something, right?

30
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:33,880
If Chief Ohara catches you,
you'll get scolded.

31
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:36,240
Those shopping district guys

32
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:39,120
are plotting to snatch my bonus!

33
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,980
We came so close last year, didn't we?

34
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,660
N-no way, senpai?

35
00:02:43,660 --> 00:02:44,840
You're bugging us?

36
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,020
Don't say such nasty things.

37
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:50,600
When I went to the model shop
yesterday to return a defective item,

38
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:56,620
I found a small bug inside the box,
one someone made just for fun.

39
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,680
So, you could say it's an act of God.

40
00:03:00,240 --> 00:03:01,440
That's totally on purpose.

41
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:02,140
Yeah, right.

42
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:05,440
It's your fault, Ryo-chan,
for never paying back your debts.

43
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:08,060
Why don't you just pay them back for once?

44
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,520
Nobody said I wasn't going to pay them back.

45
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:14,340
I've already decided what to buy
with this year's bonus, though.

46
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:21,540
It's the world's first humanoid household bipedal robot,
Robot-kun!

47
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:24,680
The one that was all over TV, right?

48
00:03:25,380 --> 00:03:29,000
Since it was a limited run,
the competition was insane.

49
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:31,160
But I somehow managed to
get a purchase voucher.

50
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:33,520
All that's left is to transfer the payment.

51
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:38,960
By the way, Sagonji applied for
the ultra-limited Saori version.

52
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:43,660
He paid with his salary from the other day,
so it should arrive soon.

53
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:45,900
What do you plan to do
with something like that?

54
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:48,560
It's bound to become a burden right away,
you know.

55
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:53,060
Shut up! Before the 21st century even arrives,
a robot is coming into our home!

56
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,520
Don't you think that's amazing?

57
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:57,080
It doesn't have to be in Ryo-chan's house!

58
00:03:57,400 --> 00:03:59,740
Don't you understand a man's dream?

59
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,400
Debt repayment over dreams!

60
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:04,380
So, what's the plan this time?

61
00:04:04,860 --> 00:04:06,640
Tch! That's the crucial part.

62
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:10,600
But before that,
there's something I want to tell everyone.

63
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:15,080
What's wrong? You look unusually serious.

64
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:16,620
Did something happen?

65
00:04:20,680 --> 00:04:22,420
I'm retiring!

66
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:24,840
What!?

67
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,760
What's going on, senpai?

68
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:31,380
W-what do you mean, retiring? Plum-ya-san!

69
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,340
Retiring?

70
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:38,040
I'm thinking of closing up shop
and moving out to the countryside.

71
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:40,960
A-are you serious?

72
00:04:41,080 --> 00:04:43,540
You're not old enough to retire yet!

73
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:44,660
But why?

74
00:04:45,900 --> 00:04:48,540
To be honest, lately, my wife has been...

75
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:50,200
My shop has been running
at a loss for a long time.

76
00:04:52,100 --> 00:04:55,820
With video games taking over, model kits
just aren't selling at all these days.

77
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,000
Today...

78
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:08,180
You started this shop out of your love for model kits,
after all.

79
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:10,540
And you don't even feel like selling it off.

80
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:13,220
So I figured you might
as well go all the way.

81
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,320
Isn't giving up a little too quickly?

82
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:18,720
Where has your usual tenacity gone?

83
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,740
That's right.

84
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:22,780
Who else but the Plum-ya owner
could go up against Ryo-san?

85
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:25,440
Every shop is struggling, you know.

86
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,020
Let's hang in there a little longer.

87
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:31,740
I've been hanging in there too, even though
my wife has tried to leave me more than once.

88
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:32,160
Right?

89
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,280
He's already made up his mind.

90
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:38,460
Plum-ya-san.

91
00:05:39,420 --> 00:05:40,780
That's all I have to say.

92
00:05:41,180 --> 00:05:43,320
Well, let's resume our strategy meeting.

93
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:46,640
He's going to be gone.

94
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:51,780
Shouldn't we tell Ryo-san
about what we just heard?

95
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:53,060
Y-yeah, you're right.

96
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,540
Ryo-san isn't a demon, you know.

97
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:58,180
If he hears that Plum-ya is retiring,

98
00:05:58,180 --> 00:06:00,480
he might let us have this one.

99
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:01,460
R-right.

100
00:06:02,020 --> 00:06:03,800
Let's at least get him to give up on that.

101
00:06:03,800 --> 00:06:04,700
B-but...

102
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,540
That's exactly why it's the last one.

103
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:09,060
I want a fair, square fight with Ryo-san.

104
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:10,500
No handicap, mind you.

105
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:14,400
Keep my retirement just between us,
will you?

106
00:06:15,460 --> 00:06:19,620
I don't want Ryo-san to hear
about it and go easy on me.

107
00:06:21,200 --> 00:06:23,640
Plum-ya, you're a real man.

108
00:06:28,160 --> 00:06:30,920
I can't believe Plum-ya is retiring.

109
00:06:31,500 --> 00:06:34,560
Senior,
this time we have to let him have the win.

110
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:38,820
Don't joke around. He himself said
he didn't want any special treatment!

111
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:47,660
This is his last chance, Reiko. You can buy robots anytime, right?
But it's a limited edition! Besides, we don't even know if he'll ever come back.

112
00:06:47,660 --> 00:07:10,480
So it's still my bonus after all. I can
spend it however I like. Got a problem?

113
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,340
Aaaaaaah!

114
00:07:21,340 --> 00:07:22,260
Aaaaaaah!

115
00:07:23,820 --> 00:07:29,960
Hold on, this year I'm really getting that bonus!
I'm already sick of hearing about sabo-zerī!

116
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:34,200
This year for sure, this year for sure...
Kāta shikozo.

117
00:07:41,240 --> 00:07:58,540
Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes!
Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes! Here it comes!

118
00:07:58,540 --> 00:08:00,440
Hurry up and make it do something!

119
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:01,700
You'll be amazed.

120
00:08:01,700 --> 00:08:02,560
Saori!

121
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:05,020
What? Tatcha?

122
00:08:06,080 --> 00:08:06,940
Saori!

123
00:08:08,060 --> 00:08:09,620
It just answered, that's all!

124
00:08:09,620 --> 00:08:10,960
It answered, that's all.

125
00:08:10,960 --> 00:08:13,440
This was the dream of every Documemo fan,

126
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:16,180
having a flesh-and-blood
Saori call your name.

127
00:08:16,180 --> 00:08:17,840
Even if it's a robot.

128
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:19,680
No, it's the real Saori.

129
00:08:19,680 --> 00:08:21,100
Totally different.

130
00:08:21,100 --> 00:08:24,580
Hey, it's not just a
robot that answers, is it?

131
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:26,880
Of course not.

132
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:31,980
Hey, Saori, tea!

133
00:08:31,980 --> 00:08:33,820
Got it, Tacchan.

134
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,200
Here you go.

135
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:39,940
Thanks, Saori.

136
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:43,200
The movements are smoother than I expected.

137
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:46,240
Hey, make it do something else too.

138
00:08:46,720 --> 00:08:48,820
Then, Saori, one more tea.

139
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:52,020
Got it, Tacchan. Here you go.

140
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:54,780
Thanks, Saori.

141
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,680
Isn't that the same as before?

142
00:08:58,540 --> 00:09:01,820
Look. Saori, two more teas.

143
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:08,880
Got it, Wa-chan, here you go.
Wow, that's amazing. Thanks, Saori.

144
00:09:10,520 --> 00:09:17,940
Hey, you don't mean it can only do this much, do you?
Well, it only arrived today.

145
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:23,980
It still has a lot of troublesome settings to sort out.
Hey, Saori, clean the room.

146
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,740
Saori doesn't understand.

147
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:29,860
Then, Saori, massage my shoulders.

148
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,360
Saori doesn't understand.

149
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:35,966
Saori, try clapping. Saori,

150
00:09:36,016 --> 00:09:39,920
Try doing the tongue-twister thing.
Saori, pick your nose.

151
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:42,661
Saori doesn't understand.

152
00:09:42,711 --> 00:09:46,060
Saori doesn't understand.
Saori doesn't understand.

153
00:09:46,540 --> 00:09:49,960
This is the same as it not being able to do anything at all.
It's like it's about to...

154
00:09:49,960 --> 00:09:51,580
Stop it! It was expensive!

155
00:09:51,880 --> 00:09:54,200
This is no different from
a plain tea-serving doll!

156
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,180
Something like that has
existed since the Edo period!

157
00:09:56,400 --> 00:09:58,420
Calm down, Ryotsu. Look at that.

158
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,420
There's a manual this thick, you know.

159
00:10:01,800 --> 00:10:04,380
Just programming one
movement is a real hassle.

160
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:08,460
Good grief.
Do I have to read all of that too?

161
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,200
So, shall we cancel?

162
00:10:10,520 --> 00:10:11,180
Cancel?

163
00:10:12,480 --> 00:10:15,480
If we cancel, the whole bonus is left over.

164
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:19,000
Now, now, why show mercy here?
Kankichi Ryotsu!

165
00:10:19,980 --> 00:10:21,140
W-what's wrong?

166
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:23,240
I'm not canceling, you hear me!

167
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,240
I'm definitely going to buy it!

168
00:10:25,540 --> 00:10:26,940
A-all right, all right!

169
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:38,860
Ryo-san, are you there?
You've got a visitor.

170
00:10:39,080 --> 00:10:39,560
Right.

171
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,720
It's you lot!

172
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:50,680
Actually, Plum-ya told us to keep quiet about this,
but

173
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:54,260
we really felt you needed to hear it.

174
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:58,840
Actually,
after the bonus showdown with Plum-ya,

175
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,800
I'm busy.

176
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,860
I don't have time to deal with you lot.

177
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:06,380
Just listen, Ryo-san.

178
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:09,740
Plum-ya is...

179
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,340
I said I'm busy!

180
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:13,160
Go away.

181
00:11:14,960 --> 00:11:18,520
Fine. We'd better leave it for today.

182
00:11:18,940 --> 00:11:19,580
Yeah, you're right.

183
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:21,700
Sorry to bother you.

184
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,060
Tomorrow's a mess,
so come back the day after tomorrow.

185
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:50,780
Understood. I'll call tomorrow
to confirm the time. Goodbye.

186
00:11:52,180 --> 00:11:53,240
Good work!

187
00:11:55,140 --> 00:11:59,640
This one, that... Yoyo-sa.

188
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:12,920
What happened? Your shelves are all empty! I
was just thinking of tidying up a bit. I see.

189
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,220
Found it, this is it, this is it.

190
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,240
What's this?

191
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:19,960
It's the one Ryo-san wanted.

192
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:24,720
This is a promotional figure, isn't it?

193
00:12:24,720 --> 00:12:27,340
Collectors would pay 100,000 yen for this.

194
00:12:27,860 --> 00:12:29,940
You said you'd never let it go.

195
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:30,980
Why?

196
00:12:31,480 --> 00:12:33,300
Keeping it just takes up space.

197
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:35,720
It's better to give it to
someone who wants it, right?

198
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:37,620
I'm not going to charge you for it.

199
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:38,820
Don't worry.

200
00:12:41,340 --> 00:12:42,180
Plum-ya.

201
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:47,680
But you'll pay off all your past
tabs with this bonus, got it?

202
00:12:47,680 --> 00:12:49,380
I know.

203
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:21,920
Before the run, in position.

204
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:25,460
In front of Shichara-ka Bank, in position.

205
00:13:26,340 --> 00:13:28,800
This is Nikoniko Dormitory, in position.

206
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:31,220
Katsushika-shi-o-mae,
in position, confirmed.

207
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:31,860
Yeah.

208
00:13:32,280 --> 00:13:34,500
This is it, Plum-ya-san.

209
00:13:36,460 --> 00:13:38,960
You, once this match is over -

210
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:42,660
Granny, just for today,
let me focus on this match.

211
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:43,740
Please.

212
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:47,760
Plum-ya-san, you're a real man.

213
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:50,840
Attention, all personnel.

214
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:52,960
Based on information from a reliable source,

215
00:13:52,960 --> 00:13:56,820
it has been confirmed that
Ryo-san's bonus payment date is today.

216
00:13:57,260 --> 00:14:00,440
Since last year, Ryo-san's bonus
has been paid by bank transfer.

217
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,380
But given his personality,

218
00:14:02,380 --> 00:14:05,240
he's sure to withdraw the entire
amount from his account right away.

219
00:14:05,240 --> 00:14:07,960
We must not miss that
opening and take it all!

220
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:12,420
We must win this bonus battle at all costs.

221
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:14,820
I wish you all the best of luck.

222
00:14:14,820 --> 00:14:15,540
That's all.

223
00:14:16,280 --> 00:14:19,080
No matter what, I'll catch Ryo-san.

224
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:21,480
For Plum-ya-san,

225
00:14:21,880 --> 00:14:23,300
this is his last year, after all.

226
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:27,560
This year, it's for Plum-ya,
not for our own interests.

227
00:14:32,920 --> 00:14:33,880
Excuse me for a moment.

228
00:14:36,100 --> 00:14:37,080
Let me see your face.

229
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,560
Uh, wrong person!

230
00:14:41,960 --> 00:14:42,640
I see.

231
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:47,280
Hold on a second.

232
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:50,400
Let's see what's in that package.

233
00:14:50,400 --> 00:14:51,200
This one?

234
00:14:51,780 --> 00:14:53,560
W-what is this?

235
00:14:53,560 --> 00:14:56,500
It was all over the TV, wasn't it?

236
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:59,020
It's a life-sized bipedal robot!

237
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:00,220
So this is it.

238
00:15:01,260 --> 00:15:02,500
Alright, you can go.

239
00:15:02,500 --> 00:15:03,060
Yeah.

240
00:15:06,140 --> 00:15:07,400
What a bunch of idiots.

241
00:15:07,400 --> 00:15:09,840
Not even noticing that I'm right here.

242
00:15:11,440 --> 00:15:12,080
See ya.

243
00:15:16,540 --> 00:15:17,180
Ryo-san

244
00:15:17,180 --> 00:15:19,300
You haven't done anything weird to Saori,
have you?

245
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:20,180
As if I would.

246
00:15:20,660 --> 00:15:23,240
If you think so,
hurry up and head to the bank.

247
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,040
Saori.

248
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,580
I'm her mother, after all.

249
00:15:29,460 --> 00:15:30,380
That's strange.

250
00:15:30,860 --> 00:15:31,980
Knowing Ryo-san,

251
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,280
I figured he'd head
straight there first thing.

252
00:15:36,240 --> 00:15:38,900
Nikoniko, has he made any move yet?

253
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:39,840
Not yet.

254
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,260
Did anyone come out?

255
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:45,480
A big guy, some kind of judo instructor.

256
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,300
The one who helped us last year.

257
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:48,720
Sakonji?

258
00:15:48,720 --> 00:15:49,340
Yeah, that's the one.

259
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,780
Was he carrying any package?

260
00:15:53,240 --> 00:15:55,140
We checked the contents, though.

261
00:15:55,140 --> 00:15:57,000
It was a life-size robot.

262
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,200
A life-size robot?!

263
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:01,360
Split into two teams
and charge in right away.

264
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:04,680
I'm on my way too.

265
00:16:04,680 --> 00:16:05,980
What's wrong?

266
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:08,180
Ryo-san may have already escaped.

267
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:21,680
Well? Looks like he's in there.

268
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:22,280
What?

269
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,640
Shut up! I'm sleepy!

270
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,880
Come on, that's ridiculous.

271
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:32,960
Shut up! I'm sleepy!

272
00:16:34,800 --> 00:16:36,900
Ryo-san! Ryo-san! Ryo-san!

273
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:37,600
Hey, Plum-ya!

274
00:16:37,720 --> 00:16:39,560
Shut up! I'm sleepy!

275
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:44,180
You can fool the others,
but you can't fool me.

276
00:16:45,580 --> 00:16:46,600
Plum-ya!

277
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,180
Shut up! I'm sleepy!

278
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,300
Shut up! I'm sleepy!

279
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:52,640
Just as I thought.

280
00:16:52,640 --> 00:16:53,760
Shut up! I'm sleepy!

281
00:16:53,760 --> 00:16:55,460
Contact the people in front
of the bank immediately!

282
00:16:55,860 --> 00:16:56,860
Ryo-san's coming!

283
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:02,360
He's coming, Ryo-san is!

284
00:17:02,360 --> 00:17:04,740
Here he comes, Ryo-san!

285
00:17:12,680 --> 00:17:13,560
Look!

286
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:15,860
Don't let him get away!

287
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,160
This is our final showdown.

288
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:20,200
We're definitely going to catch him.

289
00:17:26,320 --> 00:17:27,440
Saori!

290
00:17:28,060 --> 00:17:29,600
Come on, give up already.

291
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:30,660
Ooh-chan!

292
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:32,980
He's not here!

293
00:17:33,620 --> 00:17:35,580
What? No way!

294
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:39,620
Right, he can't have gotten that far yet.

295
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,720
Search every nook and cranny.

296
00:17:42,620 --> 00:17:45,380
It looks like Ryo-san got away.
Let's go too.

297
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:45,940
Yeah.

298
00:17:58,300 --> 00:17:59,200
Yes!

299
00:18:00,280 --> 00:18:03,420
Good thing we changed his bank account.

300
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:09,220
Did he withdraw his whole bonus?

301
00:18:09,220 --> 00:18:11,900
What's in my breast pocket is...

302
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:16,440
Plum-ya, why is this here?

303
00:18:17,580 --> 00:18:19,960
We found this in Ryo-san's room.

304
00:18:19,960 --> 00:18:22,060
That's when it clicked.

305
00:18:22,460 --> 00:18:24,540
Damn it, I'm not getting caught!

306
00:18:24,540 --> 00:18:25,120
Tch.

307
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:25,940
Foolish.

308
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:31,680
Do you think you can get away?

309
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:33,660
With a snowmobile...

310
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:38,520
I prepared for something like this.

311
00:18:38,520 --> 00:18:39,960
You'd better be prepared.

312
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:44,500
Damn it!

313
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:50,640
Without courage like this, you can't show your usual strength!
Give up!

314
00:18:53,380 --> 00:18:54,320
Get him!

315
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:02,300
Stop!

316
00:19:11,980 --> 00:19:13,520
Why are you coming this way!

317
00:19:21,300 --> 00:19:22,580
Ow ow!

318
00:19:23,360 --> 00:19:25,100
My bonus...

319
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:28,680
Plum-ya

320
00:19:29,980 --> 00:19:31,000
Hey, are you all right?

321
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:33,840
Ryo-san, is that you?

322
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,480
Looks like I sprained my ankle.

323
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,940
I can't chase you any further.

324
00:19:38,940 --> 00:19:40,180
Plum-ya

325
00:19:40,960 --> 00:19:43,400
In the end, I couldn't beat you, Ryo-san.

326
00:19:43,940 --> 00:19:44,940
It's a shame.

327
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:46,640
Plum-ya

328
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:47,720
You...

329
00:19:48,380 --> 00:19:50,640
But I have no regrets.

330
00:19:51,340 --> 00:19:55,140
I got to fight with all my strength
against an opponent like this.

331
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:57,720
It's the pride of my life.

332
00:19:58,780 --> 00:19:59,880
Thank you, Ryo-san.

333
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:01,480
Plum-ya!

334
00:20:05,860 --> 00:20:07,560
Ow ow

335
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:09,500
What happened, Ryo-san?

336
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:12,780
Looks like the shock of his
debts broke every bone in his body.

337
00:20:12,780 --> 00:20:14,940
We have to get him to a hospital right away.

338
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:16,060
Ryo-san?

339
00:20:17,720 --> 00:20:20,460
My bonus should be lying
around here somewhere, though.

340
00:20:21,180 --> 00:20:21,860
What a shame.

341
00:20:21,860 --> 00:20:23,520
Truly a shame.

342
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,620
Ryo-san.

343
00:20:26,620 --> 00:20:29,000
Even if you go back to the countryside,

344
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:30,660
take care of yourself and live well.

345
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:33,260
Countryside? What are you talking about?

346
00:20:33,260 --> 00:20:33,580
Right?

347
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,040
Sorry, Saori...

348
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:42,480
for putting you through this...

349
00:20:43,520 --> 00:20:45,160
Come back to life, Saori!

350
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,600
Got it, Dacchan.

351
00:20:49,520 --> 00:20:50,380
Saori...

352
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:52,060
Hey!

353
00:20:53,100 --> 00:20:53,940
Where are you going?

354
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:54,780
Saori...

355
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:58,480
That's...

356
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:02,380
We actually caught Ryo-san!

357
00:21:02,380 --> 00:21:04,560
This is Plum-ya's victory through sheer determination,
isn't it?

358
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:07,080
You really are a man, after all.

359
00:21:07,080 --> 00:21:08,880
I'm going out to earn some money now.

360
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:14,620
So your claim that you were retiring
to the countryside was a complete lie?

361
00:21:15,260 --> 00:21:18,820
I'm sure I never said
anything like that to Ryo-san.

362
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:20,820
But the shop...

363
00:21:21,380 --> 00:21:23,300
was just preparing for renovations.

364
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:26,460
Lately, games sell better than plastic models,
you know.

365
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:31,340
I wonder why he thought I was retiring.

366
00:21:31,340 --> 00:21:33,180
Did he bug the shop or something?

367
00:21:33,180 --> 00:21:37,340
So he realized we were bugged
and played along with the act?

368
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,980
That's dirty! Are the others coming too?

369
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:42,080
No, none of them know about it.

370
00:21:42,080 --> 00:21:45,700
They say you have to fool your allies
first if you want to deceive the enemy.

371
00:21:46,520 --> 00:21:50,160
So the retirement story was a complete lie?

372
00:21:50,480 --> 00:21:53,880
That reminds me,
the model shop's father and grandfather

373
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:55,540
ran a shop at that location.

374
00:21:55,540 --> 00:21:57,620
They're born-and-bred Edo folk.

375
00:21:57,620 --> 00:22:00,880
Then there's no way you have a countryside hometown,
is there?

376
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,420
You tricked me, didn't you!

377
00:22:02,420 --> 00:22:05,140
Shut up, it's your fault for getting fooled!

378
00:22:05,140 --> 00:22:07,980
Alright,
this year I'm finally getting my bonus!

379
00:22:08,540 --> 00:22:09,260
Me?

380
00:22:09,260 --> 00:22:23,960


381
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:26,140
Come on, weren't you supposed
to have sprained your ankle?

382
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:28,920
Ryo-san, you're the one in trouble all over,
aren't you?!

383
00:22:29,080 --> 00:22:30,380
Saoriii!

384
00:22:30,900 --> 00:22:31,960
Stop right there!

385
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:33,820
Saoriii!

386
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:50,040
Where did he go?

387
00:22:51,380 --> 00:22:52,220
Saori!

388
00:22:53,960 --> 00:22:54,280
Dai-chan

389
00:22:55,320 --> 00:22:56,320
There!

390
00:23:03,600 --> 00:23:05,300
Stop the machine right now!

391
00:23:05,640 --> 00:23:07,200
W-what is this, you guys!

392
00:23:07,280 --> 00:23:08,540
What happened!

393
00:23:11,780 --> 00:23:15,760
M-my bonus has been shredded into chips!

394
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:18,020
Come on, Gonji, this is your fault!

395
00:23:19,420 --> 00:23:20,380
Saori

396
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:23,340
Why are you too?

397
00:23:24,480 --> 00:23:27,180
He's too pitiful.
I can't even bring myself to be angry.

398
00:23:27,180 --> 00:23:28,180
Yeah, you're right.

399
00:23:28,180 --> 00:23:30,820
Then can we be the ones who get angry?

400
00:23:30,820 --> 00:23:33,880
How dare you interfere, Plum-ya!

401
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:37,780
We had no choice. We had to take his bonus.

402
00:23:37,780 --> 00:23:39,880
It's all Ryo-san's fault to begin with.

403
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:42,180
Wasn't it you who lied?

404
00:23:42,180 --> 00:23:43,580
Plum-ya.

405
00:23:43,580 --> 00:23:44,720
Ryo-san.

406
00:23:50,800 --> 00:23:55,280
Ryo-san, next year,
next year, I'll definitely win!

407
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:58,360
Honestly, you should just retire already.

408
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:05,500
What on earth happened?

409
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:07,840
People and cars are all frozen!

410
00:24:07,840 --> 00:24:10,340
It's as if time has stopped.

411
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:12,420
What are you guys?

412
00:24:12,420 --> 00:24:14,900
Don't tell me he's an alien or something.

413
00:24:15,360 --> 00:24:17,120
Next time: Time, stop!

414
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:19,640
This is Japan, you know!

